red as meliodas  fighting alongside a brand new hero like  percival who is still only discovering  the extent of his power but raising the  stakes in terms of power wouldn't be  such a bad idea because again i feel  like a lot of fans of the original want  to see the kind of insane battles that  we saw in the original series but we are  still of course only on chapter 51 of  the sequel the original had over 300  chapters so we have to brace ourselves  that said having someone like melioda  step in for at least a little while and  impress everybody with his exceptional  demon power would be extremely epic  let me know what you guys think are you  as hyped as i am that meliodas is back  and did you like the fact that he is  still basically the same guy or would  you have preferred it if he had changed  more over the years what do you think  meliotis's relationship with percival's  grandpa was and what are his true  intentions with the four knights of the  apocalypse finally is meliodas about to  become a regular in the sequel or is  this just a temporary situation don't  forget to leave your feedback down in  the comments below if you guys enjoyed  this video and you want to see more  seven of these sins and four nights of  the apocalypse content on the channel  don't forget to leave a like it only  takes a second but it helps a lot and if  you're new here or maybe you watch our  videos but you just haven't taken the  time to subscribe yet do me a quick  favor and make this the video that you  subscribe and hit that notification bell  to turn on all notifications it seems  like a small thing but subscribing  actually helps me out a lot on youtube  you can also hit me up on twitter and  instagram at  uproar as always thank you guys so much  for watching and until next time see ya  space cowboys

